{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-virtual"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular Virtual supports Angular 19 and newer. In practice, the adapter is intended to support Angular LTS releases and newer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"injectvirtualizer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectVirtualizer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function injectVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    Omit<VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>, 'getScrollElement'>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n  > & { scrollElement: ElementRef<TScrollElement> | TScrollElement | undefined },\n): AngularVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function returns an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularVirtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":" instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThe returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularVirtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":" mirrors the core "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Virtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":", but adapter-managed state is exposed through Angular signals. This includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getTotalSize"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getVirtualItems"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isScrolling"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"range"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollDirection"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollElement"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollOffset"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollRect"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measurementsCache"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"injectwindowvirtualizer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectWindowVirtualizer"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function injectWindowVirtualizer<TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    VirtualizerOptions<Window, TItemElement>,\n    | 'getScrollElement'\n    | 'observeElementRect'\n    | 'observeElementOffset'\n    | 'scrollToFn'\n  >,\n): AngularVirtualizer<Window, TItemElement>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function returns a window-based "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularVirtualizer"},{"type":"text","value":" instance configured to work with the window as the scrollElement."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"injectvirtualizer","text":"injectVirtualizer","level":2},{"id":"injectwindowvirtualizer","text":"injectWindowVirtualizer","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/angular-virtual` adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic.\n\nAngular Virtual supports Angular 19 and newer. In practice, the adapter is intended to support Angular LTS releases and newer.\n\n## `injectVirtualizer`\n\n```ts\nfunction injectVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    Omit<VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>, 'getScrollElement'>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n  > & { scrollElement: ElementRef<TScrollElement> | TScrollElement | undefined },\n): AngularVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement>\n```\n\nThis function returns an `AngularVirtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThe returned `AngularVirtualizer` mirrors the core `Virtualizer`, but adapter-managed state is exposed through Angular signals. This includes:\n\n- `getTotalSize`\n- `getVirtualItems`\n- `isScrolling`\n- `options`\n- `range`\n- `scrollDirection`\n- `scrollElement`\n- `scrollOffset`\n- `scrollRect`\n- `measurementsCache`\n\n## `injectWindowVirtualizer`\n\n```ts\nfunction injectWindowVirtualizer<TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    VirtualizerOptions<Window, TItemElement>,\n    | 'getScrollElement'\n    | 'observeElementRect'\n    | 'observeElementOffset'\n    | 'scrollToFn'\n  >,\n): AngularVirtualizer<Window, TItemElement>\n```\n\nThis function returns a window-based `AngularVirtualizer` instance configured to work with the window as the scrollElement.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Angular Virtual\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-virtual` adapter is a wrapper around the core virtual logic.\n\nAngular Virtual supports Angular 19 and newer. In practice, the adapter is intended to support Angular LTS releases and newer.\n\n## `injectVirtualizer`\n\n```ts\nfunction injectVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    Omit<VirtualizerOptions<TScrollElement, TItemElement>, 'getScrollElement'>,\n    'observeElementRect' | 'observeElementOffset' | 'scrollToFn'\n  > & { scrollElement: ElementRef<TScrollElement> | TScrollElement | undefined },\n): AngularVirtualizer<TScrollElement, TItemElement>\n```\n\nThis function returns an `AngularVirtualizer` instance configured to work with an HTML element as the scrollElement.\nThe returned `AngularVirtualizer` mirrors the core `Virtualizer`, but adapter-managed state is exposed through Angular signals. This includes:\n\n- `getTotalSize`\n- `getVirtualItems`\n- `isScrolling`\n- `options`\n- `range`\n- `scrollDirection`\n- `scrollElement`\n- `scrollOffset`\n- `scrollRect`\n- `measurementsCache`\n\n## `injectWindowVirtualizer`\n\n```ts\nfunction injectWindowVirtualizer<TItemElement = unknown>(\n  options: PartialKeys<\n    VirtualizerOptions<Window, TItemElement>,\n    | 'getScrollElement'\n    | 'observeElementRect'\n    | 'observeElementOffset'\n    | 'scrollToFn'\n  >,\n): AngularVirtualizer<Window, TItemElement>\n```\n\nThis function returns a window-based `AngularVirtualizer` instance configured to work with the window as the scrollElement.\n"}
